B=\\frac{3}{4}.$ Therefore, the period is $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{2\\pi }{\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)}=\\frac{8\\pi }{3}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186253370 :question/worked-solution "Given a function in the form $y=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=\\frac{4}{3}.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)}={270}^{∘}.$" "Given a function in the form $y=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=\\frac{4}{3}.$ Therefore, the period is $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{{360}^{∘}}{\\left(\\frac{4}{3}\\right)}={270}^{∘}.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186253373 :question/problem "Which expression gives all of the zeros of $y=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{4})?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." "Which expression gives all of the zeros of $$\n\\displaystyle y=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{4})?\n$$ Assume that $n$ is an integer."] [:db/cas 17592186253375 :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ Which expression gives all of the values of $x$ at which $f(x)$ attains its maximum value? Assume that $n$ is an integer." "Consider the function $$\n\\displaystyle f(x)=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}).\n$$ Which expression gives all of the values of $x$ at which $f(x)$ attains its maximum value? Assume that $n$ is an integer."] [:db/cas 17592186253377 :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ Which expression gives all of the values of $x$ at which $f(x)$ attains its minimum value? Assume that $n$ is an integer." "Consider the function $$\n\\displaystyle f(x)=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{3}).\n$$ Which expression gives all of the values of $x$ at which $f(x)$ attains its minimum value? Assume that $n$ is an integer."] [:db/cas 1759218